BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Harvest Fest to Benefit Coffee Farmers
DTSTART:20260830T150000
DTEND:20260830T180000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:c1e53c6c18b30d81b84340615acf93@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:More bands\, a new location\, an online silent auction and foo
 d truck flavors will mark the fifth annual Food 4 Farmers Harvest Festival
  fundraiser on Sunday\, August 30 in Shelburne\, Vermont. For the first ti
 me\, the Harvest Festival will be held from 3-6 pm at the scenic Shelburne
  Orchards on Orchard Road -- a quintessentially Vermont pick-your-own farm
 . Families will enjoy Cuban/Brazilian music from Los Songoros and folk-roc
 k tunes from the Traveling Middleburys and Albany Sound\, all while being 
 surrounded by this year’s crop of peaches and apples. There will also be
  delicious wood-fired pizza available from Pizza 44 and Venezuelan soul fo
 od from The Caracas food truck. Brandy tastings will be held at Shelburne 
 Orchard’s on-site distillery. Tickets are $25 at www.food4farmers.org an
 d include a token for beer\, wine or a soda and ice cream from The Scoop. 
 Children under 12 get in free and can enjoy the bouncy house\, lawn games 
 and tractor rides. Families are encouraged to bring their own chairs or bl
 ankets as seating will be limited.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Shelburne Orchards\, 216 Orchard Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/annual-har
 vest-fest-to-benefit-coffee-farmers-25-08-2026-16-05-12
END:VEVENT
