DESCRIPTION:Bandwagon Summer Series: Homegrown Festival comes to West Rive
 r Park in Brattleboro on Sunday\, Aug. 30\, celebrating the best of southe
 rn Vermont's homegrown talent with an afternoon of music\, circus arts\, a
 nd family fun. Headliners The Gaslight Tinkers blend Afro-Caribbean rhythm
 s\, funk\, reggae\, and Celtic influences into an irresistible dance party
 . The New England Center for Circus Arts (NECCA) showcases dazzling aerial
 ists and acrobats\, while Zara Bodé's Little Big Band brings timeless swi
 ng\, jazz\, and vintage country classics to the stage. Gates open at 3 p.m
 .\, show at 4 p.m. Food from Mama T's Sweet Spot and AlpineGlo Farm Taquer
 ia\, plus refreshments and a bar. Kids under 12 are free. Bring a blanket 
 or chair. Sponsored in part by Southern Vermont Solar.\n\nSources: Vermont
  Public
LOCATION:West River Park\, 333 W River Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/bandwagon-
 summer-series-homegrown-festival-27-07-2026-20-57-45
END:VEVENT
