BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Braintree Bluegrass Brunch: Ida Mae Specker & Friends (feat. squar
 e dances called by Sarah Gibson)
DTSTART:20260830T100000
DTEND:20260830T150000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:3dc8c3a969a848aa7bba10abcd0dd0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Braintree Hill Meetinghouse Sunday\, August 30t
 h for live music\, bike rides\, food\, and family fun! Ida Mae Specker\, d
 aughter of John Specker\, brings Vermont’s folk traditions to life throu
 gh old-time fiddle music\, heartfelt vocals\, and intergenerational musici
 anship. Blending traditional and contemporary folk influences shaped by st
 orytelling\, community\, and place\, her performances create an intimate a
 nd powerful musical experience rooted in American folk tradition. Special 
 guest Sarah Gibson will get the audience moving with her square dance call
 ing\, perfectly complementing Ida’s spirited performance. Event Schedule
  10 AM: Mountain bike ride with Ridgeline Outdoor Collective 11 AM: Ground
 s open 12–3 PM: Live music Food\, drink\, and select craft vendors will 
 be on site. Please leave pets at home.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Braintree Hill Meetinghouse\, 2756 Braintree Hill Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/braintree-
 bluegrass-brunch-ida-mae-specker-friends-feat-square-dances-called-by-sara
 h-gibson-04-06-2026-16-47-18
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caledonia County Fair
DTSTART:20260830T070000
DTEND:20260830T200000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:db59dcc701419dec14627923c22a67@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Caledonia County Fair takes place August 26 - 30\, 2026 in
  Lyndonville\, Vermont. In 2026\, the Fair is celebrating 180 years provid
 ing family fun with an agricultural foundation. The fair has many agricult
 ural events such as animal shows and judging\, maple sugar house\, ox show
 s and pulling\, horse pulling and many exhibits in Floral Hall. Additional
 ly\, the Caledonia County Fair has many popular events and entertainment- 
 such as live music\, truck pulls\, demo derby and a Grand Cavalcade. The m
 idway is provided by Dreamland Amusements and the rides are second to none
 . The Fairs rich history and traditions combined with modern entertainment
  provide the whole family with fun\, great food and catching up with old f
 riends. There is something for everyone to enjoy. Buy your advance sale ti
 ckets through August 26 at 4pm for just $20 which includes unlimited amuse
 ment rides\, shows\, entertainment\, parking and much more! After August 2
 6 at 4pm\, gate admissions can be purchased online OR at the fair.\n\nSour
 ces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Mountain View Park\, 1 Fairground Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/caledonia-
 county-fair-22-06-2026-14-58-20
END:VEVENT
