BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Justin Levinson w/ Josh Glass\, Marty Royle at Stage 33 Live
DTSTART:20260830T150000
DTEND:20260830T170000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:1c6f79f0ffe47827a8b01bb2269127@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Justin Levinson is an award-winning\, multi-talented singer\, 
 songwriter and musician with a penchant for lyrical whimsy\, earworm melod
 ies\, British Invasion-loving songwriting\, and erudite power-pop. His cat
 alog of songs covers territory from power-pop to country to "feel-good hea
 rtbreak"\, earning steady praise from audiences and critics. He'll be brin
 ging fellow musician Josh Glass with him... a formidable duo. Marty Royle 
 is perhaps best known as the lead singer of the popular longtime DC indie-
 rock stalwarts Washington Social Club\, which made fun\, witty power pop f
 or more than two decades. MTV ran a feature on them back when MTV was a mu
 sic channel\, and Marty once somehow made Robert Smith of The Cure laugh. 
 This will be a solo performance. Stage 33 Live is a casual and intimate in
 dustrial-rustic listening room in a former factory hosting local\, regiona
 l\, and national performances and presentations of original material. No b
 ar or kitchen\, the stage is the mission\; coffee / soda / juice / water a
 nd weird snacks available by donation. More information about the nonprofi
 t\, all-volunteer project\, and this and other upcoming events\, online at
  stage33live.com. Stage 33 Live gratefully acknowledges the help of so man
 y individuals without whom none of this would be able to happen\, and inst
 itutional support this season from The Island Corporation\, WOOL-FM\, Guil
 ford Sound\, and the Rockingham Arts & Museum Project to help fund improve
 ments and maintenance\, and generally smooth out a lot of the rough edges.
  Stage 33 Live is a 501(c)3 nonprofit organization\, and all donations are
  deductible to the fullest extent. Volunteers run the thing from stem to s
 tern.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Stage 33 Live\, 33 Bridge Street\, Bellows Falls VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/justin-lev
 inson-w-josh-glass-marty-royle-at-stage-33-live-24-08-2026-11-21-21
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury: Küf Knotz and Christine Elise
DTSTART:20260830T170000
DTEND:20260830T190000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:beb5dee969f40c305c975e57844f07@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Catamount Arts welcomes genre-defying duo Küf Knotz and Chris
 tine Elise to Dog Mountain\, Sunday\, August 30th\, to close the 2026 Levi
 tt AMP St. Johnsbury Music Series. Don’t miss the final free concert of 
 the Levitt AMP season! Live music starts at 5pm. Producer/MC Küf Knotz an
 d harpist/vocalist Christine Elise have brought their hypnotic blend of hi
 p-hop\, soul\, and classical traditions to music fans across the country. 
 The unexpected pair connected over a shared desire to create innovative\, 
 feel-good dance music fusing boom-bap era and lo-fi inspired beats with sa
 tin-smooth vocals and otherworldly harp melodies. Thanks to their inimitab
 le\, earthy style and irresistible groove\, they were profiled on a recent
  episode of “Here’s the Story\,” on PBS\, and have also been feature
 d on Sugarshack Sessions\, NPR Music\, and dance floors everywhere. Cultiv
 ating a jubilant juxtaposition between hip hop\, soul\, and classical musi
 c\, they’ve opened for acts such as Digable Planets\, Wyclef Jean\, Risi
 ng Appalachia and G.Love. Sunday’s Dog Mountain show will be their first
  Vermont appearance since 2018\, when they played Winooski as part of thei
 r very first tour. They’ve played over 800 shows since and were celebrat
 ed guests on Stereophilia’s podcast\, “Your Next Favorite Band.” Lev
 itt AMP St. Johnsbury Music Series shows at Dog Mountain are free and open
  to everyone—including dogs. Patrons are encouraged to bring a blanket o
 r a low beach chair\, sunscreen\, and water\, but leave the alcohol at hom
 e. Beer\, wine\, and cocktails will be available for purchase at the St. J
 ohnsbury Distillery beer garden on site\; bringing alcohol from off-site i
 s strictly prohibited. Patrons are welcome to pack a picnic dinner or brin
 g cash for the food trucks. Overflow parking is available at the Fairbanks
  Scales parking lot\, where RCT will shuttle passengers up to Dog Mountain
  and back. New this year\, RCT will also run a concert shuttle from the St
 . Johnsbury Welcome Center to Dog Mountain at 4pm\, and then back to the W
 elcome Center after the concert. Thanks to generous support from RCT\, shu
 ttle service to the concert venue is free of charge. In addition to monthl
 y Sunday concerts at Dog Mountain\, Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury hosts free co
 ncerts at Final Fridays block parties\, on the last Friday of June\, July
 \, and August\, in partnership with Downtown St. Johnsbury. For a full sum
 mer of free family-friendly live music\, plan to be at Dog Mountain\, ever
 y Sunday\, at 5pm\, and don’t miss Final Fridays on Railroad Street! For
  more information\, including the full line-up of Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury
  Music Series artists\, visit www.catamountarts.org or email info@catamoun
 tarts.org. To learn more about Final Fridays block parties\, featuring fre
 e family-friendly activities in downtown St. Johnsbury including live musi
 c courtesy of Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury\, visit www.discoverstjohnsbury.org
 . The Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury Music Series is supported in part by the Le
 vitt Family Foundation\, which exists to strengthen the social fabric of A
 merica. The Levitt Family Foundation partners with communities to activate
  underused outdoor spaces\, creating welcoming inclusive destinations wher
 e the power of free live music brings people together and invigorates comm
 unity life. In 2026\, the Levitt Family Foundation is supporting over 1\,0
 00 free concerts in 100+ towns and cities throughout the country\, bringin
 g joy to over a million people. In addition to supporting free concerts\, 
 the Levitt Foundation is dedicated to advancing equitable music ecosystems
  through research and partnerships. Learn more at www.levitt.org.\n\nSourc
 es: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Dog Mountain\, 143 Parks Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/levitt-amp
 -st-johnsbury-kuf-knotz-and-christine-elise-24-08-2026-15-04-30
END:VEVENT
