BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rock River Players: 'Betrayal' by Harold Pinter
DTSTART:20260830T143000
DTEND:20260830T170000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:cde6c84afba5d91df83067f2b5bda9@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Rock River Players (RRP) present Harold Pinter’s Betraya
 l as its last show of the RRP summer season August 21 to 30 at the William
 sville Hall in Williamsville\, Vt. Pinter’s 1978 drama explores the corr
 osive\, multifaceted nature of deception through a reverse-chronological l
 ove triangle. Tracing a nine-year affair between Emma\, the wife of a publ
 isher\, Robert\, and Jerry\, Robert’s best friend and a literary agent\,
  the play’s concept centers on how memory\, time\, and hidden motivation
 s erode trust. RRP’s Betrayal features Randy Lichtenwalner as Robert\, S
 ean Fitzharris as Jerry\, and Addie Mahdavi as Emma. Director & Producer: 
 Bahman Mahdavi Set Design\, Stage Manager & Assistant Director: Cherie Mor
 an Tech Director: Jess Guerrero Admission is on a sliding scale of $15 to 
 $25\, though no one will be turned away for lack of funds. Tickets are ava
 ilable at the door or by using the form below. Williamsville Hall is ADA c
 ompliant and air conditioned. Every week through Aug 30\, 2026.\n\nSources
 : Vermont Public
LOCATION:Williamsville Hall\, 30 Dover Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/rock-river
 -players-betrayal-by-harold-pinter-13-08-2026-12-56-33
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shakespeare in the Woods 2026 Season
DTSTART:20260830T193000
DTEND:20260830T213000
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:0ec9f4500cd9631df44416a3595556@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare in the Woods (SitW) is proud to announce its 6th R
 epertory Season of fierce\, cutting-edge outdoor theatre. Hailed by audien
 ces as “The best Shakespeare you’ll ever see”\, the burgeoning\, awa
 rd-winning company will present two new provocative adaptations of LEAR an
 d MERRY WIVES. Performances will occur during August 12- 30\, at venue par
 tner The Equinox Golf Resort & Spa in Manchester\, Vermont. The 2026 Seaso
 n will be one of “Chaos and Folly”\, exploring a variety of themes inc
 luding love\, control\, jealousy\, deception\, nature\, and community. Sha
 kespeare in the Woods (SitW) continues to lead the way on producing a reim
 agined Shakespeare Canon for here and now. With sharp\, urgent storytellin
 g at the core of productions\, SitW is dedicated to giving their audiences
  an experience that is entertaining\, relatable\, and immersive – stripp
 ing away the notion that one needs to be a Shakespearean expert in order t
 o attend or enjoy a show. Founded in 2019\, SitW is an outdoor theatre com
 pany committed to leading bold theatrical experimentation through a modern
 \, radical\, and gender expansive queer lens\, creating innovative and rev
 elatory adaptations of Shakespeare that invite both artist and audience to
  imagine the text as a new work entirely. To learn more about SitW & plan 
 your visit\, head to www.shakespeareinthewoods.org. Full season calendar\,
  production details\, & creative team information coming soon! Every week 
 through Aug 30\, 2026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Equinox Golf Resort & Spa\, 3567 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/shakespear
 e-in-the-woods-2026-season-17-07-2026-07-03-27
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Swan
DTSTART:20260901T190000
DTEND:20260901T204500
DTSTAMP:20260830T152327Z
UID:b34c336bf78c96e2b085d5c453907f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Electric Eye presents First of the Month Films We are pleased 
 to welcome local artist KeruBo\, who will share her latest music video for
  the song “You Are Enough\,” and participate in a conversation followi
 ng the film. Of “You Are Enough\,” KeruBo writes\, “The message is n
 ot that we are perfect\, nor that we have arrived. Rather\, it is that our
  value precedes our accomplishments. We are human beings before we are hum
 an doings.” The Wrestler whet director Darren Aronofsky’s appetite for
  sagas of obsessive performers who put their body on the line in the name 
 of show business\, but Black Swan takes this idea further and deeper\, int
 o more artful\, abstract\, and terrifying territory. Natalie Portman train
 ed for months to sculpt herself into a believable ballerina and her incred
 ible commitment was duly rewarded with an Oscar win for Best Actress. Mila
  Kunis\, Vincent Cassel\, Barbara Hershey\, and Winona Ryder match her int
 ensity in this hallucinatory meta-adaptation of Tchaikovsky’s Swan Lake
 \, filtered through the backstage melodrama of All About Eve and Powell an
 d Pressburger’s The Red Shoes\, with a dose of Polanski’s Repulsion\, 
 to boot\, leaning into the inherent body horror of ballet. The story follo
 ws Nina (Portman)\, a ballerina in a New York City ballet company whose li
 fe is completely consumed with dance. She lives with her retired ballerina
  mother Erica (Hershey) who zealously supports her daughter’s profession
 al ambition. When artistic director Thomas Leroy (Cassel\, playing up the 
 George Balanchine lechery) decides to replace prima ballerina Beth MacInty
 re (Ryder) for the opening production of their new season\, Nina is his fi
 rst choice. As she sinks deeper into the duality of the central role\, and
  is drawn into the web of doppelgänger Lily (Kunis)\, her identity rapidl
 y\, and evocatively\, unravels. The Screening Room @ VTIFF 6-12\n\nSources
 : Vermont Public
LOCATION:60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/black-swan
 -18-08-2026-15-33-08
END:VEVENT
